       x2[i] += sum_j A[j][i] * y_2[j]
     We keep the original loop order (i outer, j inner) so that for
     each i the accumulation into x2[i] happens in exactly the same
     sequence as in the original code.  This preserves bit-level
     results for IEEE floating-point while still allowing us to keep
     x2[i] in a register (`xi2`) across the inner loop, eliminating
     redundant memory traffic on x2. */
  for (i = 0; i < _PB_N; i++)
    {
      DATA_TYPE xi2 = x2p[i];

      for (j = 0; j < _PB_N; j++)
        xi2 += Ap[j][i] * y2p[j];

      x2p[i] = xi2;
